customAttribute attribute_19 (
    apexlangName: clinicMaintainerCondition
    attribute: 19
    name: Shared Catalog Maintainer Condition
    type: plsqlFunctionBodyReturningBoolean
    appearance {
        sequence: 70
        attributeGroup: @sk3Clinic
    }
    help {
        helpText: Server-side PL/SQL function body returning Boolean. Required for shared maintenance. return true; permits any signed-in user with the selected Clinic Permissions. Use a role check for named maintainers, for example return apex_acl.has_user_role(p_application_id => :APP_ID, p_user_name => :APP_USER, p_role_static_id => 'CLINIC_CATALOG_ADMIN'); Checked at render and every shared write. NULL, FALSE, errors or an empty condition deny changes. Attribute 19 is preserved for existing items.
    }
)

customAttribute attribute_20 (
    apexlangName: specialtyItem
    attribute: 20
    name: Specialty Page Item
    type: pageItem
    appearance {
        sequence: 90
        attributeGroup: @sk3Skeleton
    }
    help {
        helpText: Optional page item containing a specialty code such as CARDIOLOGY, ENT or ALL. Its value overrides Specialty on initial render, and changing the page item updates the viewer. A specific specialty constrains saved anatomical areas on the server and hides the specialty switch; ALL supports records spanning specialties. Empty or unknown values use General Medicine.
    }
)

customAttribute attribute_21 (
    apexlangName: patientNameItem
    attribute: 21
    name: Name Item (Optional Fallback)
    type: pageItem
    appearance {
        sequence: 150
        attributeGroup: @sk3Clinic
    }
    help {
        helpText:
            ```
            Not required when patient.name is supplied in the patient JSON. Retained for existing integrations: optional fallback page item for the patient name. Used only when patient.name is missing from Patient Data Source. Prefer putting identity and observations together in the single JSON payload. Display & Prefill Options controls visibility and snapshots.
            ```
    }
)

customAttribute attribute_22 (
    apexlangName: patientMrnItem
    attribute: 22
    name: MR Number Item (Optional Fallback)
    type: pageItem
    appearance {
        sequence: 160
        attributeGroup: @sk3Clinic
    }
    help {
        helpText:
            ```
            Not required when patient.mrn is supplied in the patient JSON. Retained for existing integrations: optional fallback page item for the MR number. Used only when patient.mrn is missing from Patient Data Source. Prefer the unified patient JSON payload.
            ```
    }
)

customAttribute attribute_23 (
    apexlangName: contextSourceItem
    attribute: 23
    name: Patient & Observations Item
    type: pageItem
    appearance {
        sequence: 90
        attributeGroup: @sk3Clinic
    }
    help {
        helpText:
            ```
            <p>Select a hidden, textarea or other text item containing plain JSON, populated by SQL, PL/SQL, a Dynamic Action or application code. Changes to the item refresh the summary. This is a display source in APEX; saved patient snapshots and examination prefills require an authorized Static JSON, SQL or PL/SQL source.</p><p><strong>Return one patient JSON object.</strong> Include identity and observations together; omit unused fields. Complete example (fictional):</p><pre>{"patient":{"name":"Demo patient (fictional)","mrn":"DEMO-CA3D-001","id":"DEMO-001","age":42,"sex":"Male","dateOfBirth":"1984-03-10","encounterId":"VISIT-DEMO-001","details":[{"id":"department","label":"Department","value":"General medicine"},{"id":"room","label":"Room","value":"A12"}]},"recording":{"source":"Nursing intake (demo)","recordedBy":"Demo nurse","recordedAt":"2026-11-17T09:15:00+03:00"},"observations":[{"id":"bp_systolic","label":"Systolic BP","value":126,"unit":"mmHg","examField":"bp_systolic"},{"id":"bp_diastolic","label":"Diastolic BP","value":78,"unit":"mmHg","examField":"bp_diastolic"},{"id":"pulse","label":"Pulse","value":82,"unit":"beats/min","examField":"pulse"},{"id":"temperature","label":"Temperature","value":36.8,"unit":"°C","examField":"temperature","readOnly":true},{"id":"weight","label":"Weight","value":72,"unit":"kg","examField":"weight","flag":"Review","highlight":true,"note":"Example review flag supplied by the source."},{"id":"height","label":"Height","value":175,"unit":"cm","examField":"height"},{"id":"spo2","label":"Oxygen saturation","value":98,"unit":"%","examField":"spo2"},{"id":"respiratory_rate","label":"Respiratory rate","value":16,"unit":"breaths/min","examField":"respiratory_rate"},{"id":"bmi","label":"BMI","value":23.5,"unit":"kg/m²"},{"id":"glucose","label":"Blood glucose","value":5.2,"unit":"mmol/L"},{"id":"pain","label":"Pain score","value":2,"unit":"/10"},{"id":"custom_observation","label":"Your custom label","value":"Your supplied value","unit":"","source":"Your source","recordedBy":"Your recorder","recordedAt":"2026-11-17T09:15:00+03:00","flag":"","highlight":false,"readOnly":false,"hidden":true,"note":"Optional note","examField":"your_configured_exam_field"}]}</pre><p>patient: name, mrn, id, age (number in years), sex, dateOfBirth, encounterId, details (custom id/label/value/unit). recording supplies source/recordedBy/recordedAt defaults. observations require unique id and scalar value (text, number, boolean or null). Optional label, unit, flag, highlight, readOnly, hidden, note, examField and recording overrides. Preset IDs and units are in the example; custom IDs/labels are supported. Age is supplied, not calculated.</p><p>Up to 40 observations, 12 patient details and 32767 payload characters. Null/empty values do not prefill. Matching examination fields/units are prefilled only when empty; existing answers/notes/deferrals are preserved. Flags/highlights come from your source; no thresholds or conversions are inferred. Display &amp; Prefill Options controls visibility, locking and saved snapshots.</p>
            ```
    }
    dependingOn {
        attribute: @attribute_26/component
        conditionType: =
        value: ITEM
    }
)

customAttribute attribute_24 (
    apexlangName: contextOptions
    attribute: 24
    name: Display & Prefill Options (JSON)
    type: textarea
    appearance {
        sequence: 110
        attributeGroup: @sk3Clinic
    }
    default {
        value: "{}"
    }
    help {
        helpText:
            ```
            <p><strong>These are display and saving settings, not patient values.</strong> Patient values belong in Patient Data Source. Leave <code>{}</code> to use defaults. You do not need to configure this field to show supplied data.</p>
            <ul><li><code>fields</code>: visible sections/identity keys. Default: all supplied fields. Choices: name, mrn, id, age, sex, dateOfBirth, encounterId, details, observations. details appear in the Details dialog.</li>
            <li><code>labels</code>: replace identity labels, for example <code>{"mrn":"MRN","encounterId":"Encounter"}</code>.</li>
            <li><code>observationIds</code>: show only these observation IDs in the summary and Details. Omit to show all supplied observations.</li>
            <li><code>maxVisibleObservations</code>: 1–12 measurement cards above the viewer; default 6. Matching systolic/diastolic values share one BP card. The Details dialog shows the remaining visible observations without making the page taller.</li>
            <li><code>prefillExam</code>: default true. Fill empty matching examination fields from observations. False displays values without filling examination answers. Existing values, notes and deferrals are preserved.</li>
            <li><code>lockPrefilled</code>: default false. True makes all imported examination values read only. A row's readOnly can lock individual values. Notes remain editable.</li>
            <li><code>patientDataRequired</code>: false by default. True blocks editing/saving if the patient source is unavailable; saved snapshots and prefill history always require server verification.</li><li><code>saveContext</code>: default false. True saves the complete patient/observation snapshot inside the anatomy JSON. Display filters do not remove hidden data from that snapshot. A saved snapshot takes precedence when reopening a record. False omits a new snapshot; prefilled examination answers are still saved, and an existing recorded snapshot is preserved.</li></ul>
            <p>Use real JSON booleans (<code>true</code>/<code>false</code>), not quoted strings. Unknown options show a configuration message so mistakes can be corrected.</p><h3>Example</h3><pre>{
              "fields": [
                "name",
                "mrn",
                "age",
                "sex",
                "details",
                "observations"
              ],
              "labels": {
                "mrn": "MRN"
              },
              "observationIds": [
                "bp_systolic",
                "bp_diastolic",
                "pulse",
                "temperature",
                "weight",
                "height",
                "spo2",
                "respiratory_rate"
              ],
              "maxVisibleObservations": 6,
              "prefillExam": true,
              "lockPrefilled": false,
              "saveContext": true
            }</pre>
            <p>To show only patient identity, set <code>{"fields":["name","mrn","age"],"prefillExam":false}</code>. To keep defaults and save a snapshot, set <code>{"saveContext":true}</code>.</p>
            ```
    }
)

customAttribute attribute_26 (
    apexlangName: contextSourceType
    attribute: 26
    name: Patient Data Source
    type: selectList
    appearance {
        sequence: 80
        attributeGroup: @sk3Clinic
    }
    default {
        value: ITEM
    }
    help {
        helpText:
            ```
            <p><strong>Choose how to supply patient identity and observations in one JSON object.</strong></p><ul><li>Page Item containing JSON: hidden, textarea or any text item populated by SQL, PL/SQL or a Dynamic Action.</li><li>Static JSON: paste the payload.</li><li>SQL Query returning JSON: zero/one row and one VARCHAR2/CLOB JSON column.</li><li>PL/SQL Function returning JSON: function body returning JSON text/CLOB.</li><li>No live patient source: omit live data; saved snapshots can still display on review.</li></ul><p>Use each source field's Help for the complete JSON or runnable SQL/PLSQL example. All supported patient fields and observations can be supplied by every method. Optional Name/MR fallback items apply only when missing from the payload.</p><p>For SQL/PLSQL, list changing binds in Patient Items to Submit, then run await skeleton3d.get('P402_ANATOMY').refreshContext(); after changes. Clear/load the correct assessment when switching patients; refresh preserves saved data. Use current patient data explicitly replaces an old snapshot with a required amendment reason.</p>
            ```
    }
    entry item (
        sequence: 10
        display: Page Item containing JSON
        return: ITEM
    )
    entry json (
        sequence: 20
        display: Static JSON
        return: JSON
    )
    entry sql (
        sequence: 30
        display: SQL Query returning JSON
        return: SQL
    )
    entry plsql (
        sequence: 40
        display: PL/SQL Function returning JSON
        return: PLSQL
    )
    entry none (
        sequence: 60
        display: No live patient source
        return: NONE
    )
)

customAttribute attribute_27 (
    apexlangName: contextJson
    attribute: 27
    name: Patient JSON
    type: textarea
    appearance {
        sequence: 90
        attributeGroup: @sk3Clinic
    }
    dependingOn {
        attribute: @attribute_26/component
        conditionType: =
        value: JSON
    }
    help {
        helpText:
            ```
            <p>Paste your JSON object here. This uses the same contract as every other patient source.</p><p><strong>Return one patient JSON object.</strong> Include identity and observations together; omit unused fields. Complete example (fictional):</p><pre>{"patient":{"name":"Demo patient (fictional)","mrn":"DEMO-CA3D-001","id":"DEMO-001","age":42,"sex":"Male","dateOfBirth":"1984-03-10","encounterId":"VISIT-DEMO-001","details":[{"id":"department","label":"Department","value":"General medicine"},{"id":"room","label":"Room","value":"A12"}]},"recording":{"source":"Nursing intake (demo)","recordedBy":"Demo nurse","recordedAt":"2026-11-17T09:15:00+03:00"},"observations":[{"id":"bp_systolic","label":"Systolic BP","value":126,"unit":"mmHg","examField":"bp_systolic"},{"id":"bp_diastolic","label":"Diastolic BP","value":78,"unit":"mmHg","examField":"bp_diastolic"},{"id":"pulse","label":"Pulse","value":82,"unit":"beats/min","examField":"pulse"},{"id":"temperature","label":"Temperature","value":36.8,"unit":"°C","examField":"temperature","readOnly":true},{"id":"weight","label":"Weight","value":72,"unit":"kg","examField":"weight","flag":"Review","highlight":true,"note":"Example review flag supplied by the source."},{"id":"height","label":"Height","value":175,"unit":"cm","examField":"height"},{"id":"spo2","label":"Oxygen saturation","value":98,"unit":"%","examField":"spo2"},{"id":"respiratory_rate","label":"Respiratory rate","value":16,"unit":"breaths/min","examField":"respiratory_rate"},{"id":"bmi","label":"BMI","value":23.5,"unit":"kg/m²"},{"id":"glucose","label":"Blood glucose","value":5.2,"unit":"mmol/L"},{"id":"pain","label":"Pain score","value":2,"unit":"/10"},{"id":"custom_observation","label":"Your custom label","value":"Your supplied value","unit":"","source":"Your source","recordedBy":"Your recorder","recordedAt":"2026-11-17T09:15:00+03:00","flag":"","highlight":false,"readOnly":false,"hidden":true,"note":"Optional note","examField":"your_configured_exam_field"}]}</pre><p>patient: name, mrn, id, age (number in years), sex, dateOfBirth, encounterId, details (custom id/label/value/unit). recording supplies source/recordedBy/recordedAt defaults. observations require unique id and scalar value (text, number, boolean or null). Optional label, unit, flag, highlight, readOnly, hidden, note, examField and recording overrides. Preset IDs and units are in the example; custom IDs/labels are supported. Age is supplied, not calculated.</p><p>Up to 40 observations, 12 patient details and 32767 payload characters. Null/empty values do not prefill. Matching examination fields/units are prefilled only when empty; existing answers/notes/deferrals are preserved. Flags/highlights come from your source; no thresholds or conversions are inferred. Display &amp; Prefill Options controls visibility, locking and saved snapshots.</p>
            ```
    }
)

customAttribute attribute_28 (
    apexlangName: contextQuery
    attribute: 28
    name: Patient JSON Query
    type: sqlQuery
    appearance {
        sequence: 90
        attributeGroup: @sk3Clinic
    }
    validation {
        required: true
        minColumns: 1
        maxColumns: 1
    }
    dependingOn {
        attribute: @attribute_26/component
        conditionType: =
        value: SQL
    }
    help {
        helpText:
            ```
            <p><strong>Return zero/one row, exactly one JSON text column (VARCHAR2 or CLOB).</strong> Zero rows/NULL means no data. Bind page/application items normally; list changing page items in Patient Items to Submit. This runnable fictional example uses P402_PATIENT_NAME and P402_MRN; replace them with your own items or authorized query columns.</p><pre>select json_object(
              'patient' value json_object(
                'name' value :P402_PATIENT_NAME, 'mrn' value :P402_MRN,
                'id' value 'DEMO-001', 'age' value 42, 'sex' value 'Male',
                'dateOfBirth' value '1984-03-10', 'encounterId' value 'VISIT-DEMO-001',
                'details' value json_array(json_object('id' value 'department', 'label' value 'Department', 'value' value 'General medicine'))),
              'recording' value json_object('source' value 'Nursing intake (demo)',
                'recordedBy' value 'Demo nurse', 'recordedAt' value '2026-11-17T09:15:00+03:00'),
              'observations' value json_query(q'~[{"id":"bp_systolic","label":"Systolic BP","value":126,"unit":"mmHg","examField":"bp_systolic"},{"id":"bp_diastolic","label":"Diastolic BP","value":78,"unit":"mmHg","examField":"bp_diastolic"},{"id":"pulse","label":"Pulse","value":82,"unit":"beats/min","examField":"pulse"},{"id":"temperature","label":"Temperature","value":36.8,"unit":"°C","examField":"temperature","readOnly":true},{"id":"weight","label":"Weight","value":72,"unit":"kg","examField":"weight","flag":"Review","highlight":true,"note":"Example review flag supplied by the source."},{"id":"height","label":"Height","value":175,"unit":"cm","examField":"height"},{"id":"spo2","label":"Oxygen saturation","value":98,"unit":"%","examField":"spo2"},{"id":"respiratory_rate","label":"Respiratory rate","value":16,"unit":"breaths/min","examField":"respiratory_rate"}]~', '$' returning clob)
              returning clob) as patient_payload
            from dual</pre><p>Include any patient/observation keys from Patient JSON / Patient &amp; Observations Item Help. Up to 40 observations, 12 custom patient details, 32767 characters. For AJAX refresh run await skeleton3d.get('P402_ANATOMY').refreshContext();. Clear/load the correct assessment when changing patients.</p>
            ```
    }
)

customAttribute attribute_29 (
    apexlangName: contextFunction
    attribute: 29
    name: Patient JSON Function
    type: plsqlFunctionBodyReturningVarchar2
    appearance {
        sequence: 90
        attributeGroup: @sk3Clinic
    }
    dependingOn {
        attribute: @attribute_26/component
        conditionType: =
        value: PLSQL
    }
    help {
        helpText:
            ```
            <p><strong>PL/SQL function body returning one JSON object as text/CLOB.</strong> The same complete patient payload is supported by every source. Page/application item binds work normally. Replace these fictional values and P402 item names with your authorized source.</p><pre>declare
              l_payload clob;
            begin
              select json_object(
              'patient' value json_object(
                'name' value :P402_PATIENT_NAME, 'mrn' value :P402_MRN,
                'id' value 'DEMO-001', 'age' value 42, 'sex' value 'Male',
                'dateOfBirth' value '1984-03-10', 'encounterId' value 'VISIT-DEMO-001',
                'details' value json_array(json_object('id' value 'department', 'label' value 'Department', 'value' value 'General medicine'))),
              'recording' value json_object('source' value 'Nursing intake (demo)',
                'recordedBy' value 'Demo nurse', 'recordedAt' value '2026-11-17T09:15:00+03:00'),
              'observations' value json_query(q'~[{"id":"bp_systolic","label":"Systolic BP","value":126,"unit":"mmHg","examField":"bp_systolic"},{"id":"bp_diastolic","label":"Diastolic BP","value":78,"unit":"mmHg","examField":"bp_diastolic"},{"id":"pulse","label":"Pulse","value":82,"unit":"beats/min","examField":"pulse"},{"id":"temperature","label":"Temperature","value":36.8,"unit":"°C","examField":"temperature","readOnly":true},{"id":"weight","label":"Weight","value":72,"unit":"kg","examField":"weight","flag":"Review","highlight":true,"note":"Example review flag supplied by the source."},{"id":"height","label":"Height","value":175,"unit":"cm","examField":"height"},{"id":"spo2","label":"Oxygen saturation","value":98,"unit":"%","examField":"spo2"},{"id":"respiratory_rate","label":"Respiratory rate","value":16,"unit":"breaths/min","examField":"respiratory_rate"}]~', '$' returning clob)
              returning clob) into l_payload
            from dual;
              return l_payload;
            end;</pre><p>See Patient JSON / Patient &amp; Observations Item Help for every payload field. Limit: 32767 characters. For AJAX refresh, list input items in Patient Items to Submit and run await skeleton3d.get('P402_ANATOMY').refreshContext();. Clear/load the correct assessment before changing patients.</p>
            ```
    }
)

customAttribute attribute_30 (
    apexlangName: contextItemsToSubmit
    attribute: 30
    name: Patient Items to Submit
    type: pageItems
    appearance {
        sequence: 100
        attributeGroup: @sk3Clinic
    }
    help {
        helpText:
            ```
            Comma-separated page items used by the SQL/PLSQL patient source, for example P10_PATIENT_ID,P10_VISIT_ID. These values are submitted during refreshContext(). After changing them, use a Dynamic Action to run await skeleton3d.get('P10_ANATOMY').refreshContext(); Clear or load the correct assessment when switching patients; existing examination answers and saved snapshots are preserved.
            ```
    }
)

customAttribute attribute_25 (
    apexlangName: selectionGesture
    attribute: 25
    name: Select Anatomy On
    type: selectList
    appearance {
        sequence: 100
        attributeGroup: @sk3Skeleton
    }
    default {
        value: SINGLE
    }
    help {
        helpText: Choose single click/tap or double click/tap to add or open anatomy from the 3D model. Dragging never selects anatomy. Search and anatomy browser buttons remain explicit single-activation actions. Point findings and outline points still use single taps.
    }
    entry single (
        sequence: 10
        display: Single click or tap
        return: SINGLE
    )
    entry double (
        sequence: 20
        display: Double click or tap
        return: DOUBLE
    )
)

customAttribute attribute_31 (
    apexlangName: patientAuthorization
    attribute: 31
    name: Authorize Patient Access
    type: plsqlFunctionBodyReturningBoolean
    appearance {
        sequence: 110
        attributeGroup: @sk3Clinic
    }
    help {
        helpText: Optional host PL/SQL function body returning BOOLEAN. Runs before every patient source read, including render, AJAX refresh and save validation. False, null or exceptions deny access. Verify the submitted patient and encounter IDs against authenticated server context. The source query must also enforce access.
    }
)

customAttribute attribute_32 (
    apexlangName: viewerTheme
    attribute: 32
    name: Viewer Theme
    type: selectList
    appearance {
        sequence: 170
        attributeGroup: @sk3Skeleton
    }
    help {
        helpText: Follow the APEX page theme by default. System follows the operating system. Users can override and remember appearance per application and item.
    }
    default {
        value: apex
    }
    entry option1 (
        sequence: 10
        display: APEX page
        return: apex
    )
    entry option2 (
        sequence: 20
        display: System
        return: auto
    )
    entry option3 (
        sequence: 30
        display: Light
        return: light
    )
    entry option4 (
        sequence: 40
        display: Dark
        return: dark
    )
)

customAttribute attribute_33 (
    apexlangName: viewerColors
    attribute: 33
    name: Viewer Colors
    type: selectList
    appearance {
        sequence: 180
        attributeGroup: @sk3Skeleton
    }
    help {
        helpText: Default viewer colors. User preferences are stored per application and item.
    }
    default {
        value: CLINICAL
    }
    entry option1 (
        sequence: 10
        display: Clinical
        return: CLINICAL
    )
    entry option2 (
        sequence: 20
        display: Neon
        return: NEON
    )
)

customAttribute attribute_34 (
    apexlangName: neonTint
    attribute: 34
    name: Neon Tint
    type: text
    appearance {
        sequence: 190
        attributeGroup: @sk3Skeleton
    }
    help {
        helpText: Default six-digit hex color, for example #36f5ff.
    }
    default {
        value: "#36f5ff"
    }
)
